+**Outputs:**
+- Detection predictions (categories, 3D locations, centerness).
+- Rendered RGB colors $\hat{C}(\mathbf{r})$ and expected depth $D(\mathbf{r})$ for rays $\mathbf{r}$ [S1].
 
 **Data Structures:**
-*   **Detection Head:** Uses 27 location candidates per object and three convolutional layers to predict categories, locations, and centerness [S1].
-*   **NeRF Branch:** A volumetric representation learning an opacity field. Features are scattered along rays rather than fixed voxel cells, allowing for continuous geometry modeling [S1].
+The detection branch follows the ImVoxelNet architecture [S1]. It uses a voxel feature grid and a detection head with three convolutional layers to predict:
+1.  Object categories (27 location candidates per object).
+2.  3D locations (localization).
+3.  Centerness scores [S1].
 
